  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Tenant isolation",
      "description": "The claim the whole architecture rests on. A second tenant is created with the **same** administrator email, and the first tenant's token is then pointed at the second tenant's data.\n\nThe folder provisions the second tenant automatically, so any request here can be sent on its own.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Same email, two tenants, two identities",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signing in to the second tenant with credentials identical to the first, except for the slug.\n\nEmail is unique **per tenant**, not globally \u2014 so the same address is two different people here. A global unique index on email (the single-tenant default) would have made this impossible, and is very expensive to undo once real accounts exist.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"tenantSlug\": \"{{tenant2Slug}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = (() => { try { return require('atob'); } catch (x) { return atob; } })();",
                  "const c = JSON.parse(d(pm.response.json().accessToken.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')));",
                  "pm.test('resolves to a DIFFERENT user id', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(c.sub).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('userId')));",
                  "pm.test('in a DIFFERENT tenant', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(c.tenant_id).to.not.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('tenantId')));",
                  "console.log('tenant 1 admin:', pm.collectionVariables.get('userId'));",
                  "console.log('tenant 2 admin:', c.sub, '(same email, different person)');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Cross-tenant read returns 404, not 403",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{tenant2UserId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users",
                "{{tenant2UserId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A valid `TENANT_ADMIN` token from tenant one, asking for a **real** user id that belongs to tenant two.\n\nThe id exists and the caller is an administrator. The only thing stopping this is that Hibernate appended `AND tenant_id = ?` to the lookup \u2014 enforced in the mapping (`@TenantId`), not by a hand-written predicate somebody could forget.\n\n404 rather than 403 is deliberate: 403 would confirm the id belongs to somebody."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404 - the row does not exist for this tenant', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));",
                  "pm.test('and gives away nothing', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Cross-tenant write returns 404 too",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{tenant2UserId}}/roles",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users",
                "{{tenant2UserId}}",
                "roles"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Isolation is not read-only. The same restriction applies to updates, so tenant one cannot demote tenant two's administrator.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"roles\": [\n    \"TENANT_USER\"\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('404', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Each tenant lists only its own users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?size=100",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "size",
                  "value": "100"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sent with the second tenant's token. Both tenants' administrators exist in the same table; this one may see exactly one of them.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{tenant2AccessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('every row belongs to the second tenant', () =>",
                  "    b.content.forEach((u) => pm.expect(u.tenantId).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('tenant2Id'))));",
                  "pm.test('the first tenant is invisible', () =>",
                  "    pm.expect(b.content.map((u) => u.id)).to.not.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('userId')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const base = pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl');",
              "const post = (u, p) => ({ url: base + u, method: 'POST',",
              "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
              "    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify(p) } });",
              "",
              "pm.sendRequest(post('/api/v1/tenants', {",
              "    tenantName: 'Globex',",
              "    tenantSlug: pm.collectionVariables.get('tenant2Slug'),",
              "    adminEmail: pm.collectionVariables.get('email'),        // deliberately the SAME email",
              "    adminPassword: pm.collectionVariables.get('password'),",
              "    firstName: 'Grace', lastName: 'Hopper'",
              "}), () => {",
              "    pm.sendRequest(post('/api/v1/auth/login', {",
              "        tenantSlug: pm.collectionVariables.get('tenant2Slug'),",
              "        email: pm.collectionVariables.get('email'),",
              "        password: pm.collectionVariables.get('password')",
              "    }), (e, r) => {",
              "        if (e || r.code !== 200) return;",
              "        const b = r.json();",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('tenant2AccessToken', b.accessToken);",
              "        const d = (() => { try { return require('atob'); } catch (x) { return atob; } })();",
              "        const c = JSON.parse(d(b.accessToken.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')));",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('tenant2UserId', c.sub);",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('tenant2Id', c.tenant_id);",
              "    });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Refresh tokens",
      "description": "Rotation, and what happens when a token is replayed.\n\nA fresh session is established before each request, so the folder can be run on its own.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Replaying a spent token revokes the session family",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/token/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "token",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Refreshes once, then replays the token it just spent.\n\nA replayed token means two parties hold it, and there is no way to tell which one is legitimate. So the entire rotation chain is revoked \u2014 **including the successor that was valid a moment ago** (OAuth 2.0 Security BCP, RFC 9700 \u00a74.14.2). Whoever stole it loses their way back in.\n\nSigns back in at the end so the collection stays usable.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('the first refresh succeeds', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const base = pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl');",
                  "const spent = pm.collectionVariables.get('refreshToken');",
                  "const successor = pm.response.json().refreshToken;",
                  "const post = (p, cb) => pm.sendRequest({",
                  "    url: base + '/api/v1/auth/token/refresh', method: 'POST',",
                  "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
                  "    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify(p) } }, cb);",
                  "",
                  "const relogin = (cb) => pm.sendRequest({",
                  "    url: pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl') + '/api/v1/auth/login', method: 'POST',",
                  "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
                  "    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify({",
                  "        tenantSlug: pm.collectionVariables.get('tenantSlug'),",
                  "        email: pm.collectionVariables.get('email'),",
                  "        password: pm.collectionVariables.get('password')",
                  "    }) }",
                  "}, (e, r) => {",
                  "    if (!e && r.code === 200) {",
                  "        const b = r.json();",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken);",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken);",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessTokenExpiresAt', Date.now() + b.expiresIn * 1000);",
                  "    }",
                  "    if (cb) cb();",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "post({ refreshToken: spent }, (e1, replay) => {",
                  "    pm.test('the replayed token is rejected', () => pm.expect(replay.code).to.eql(401));",
                  "    post({ refreshToken: successor }, (e2, after) => {",
                  "        pm.test('and the still-valid successor dies with it', () => pm.expect(after.code).to.eql(401));",
                  "        console.log('Family revoked. Signing back in.');",
                  "        relogin();",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Logging out one device leaves the other signed in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Each login starts its own rotation family, so revocation is per device rather than per account.\n\nThis request signs in twice (a 'laptop' and a 'phone'), logs the laptop out, and shows the phone still refreshing.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"tenantSlug\": \"{{tenantSlug}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('laptop signed in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const base = pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl');",
                  "const laptop = pm.response.json();",
                  "const call = (u, p, t, cb) => pm.sendRequest({ url: base + u, method: 'POST',",
                  "    header: Object.assign({ 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, t ? { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + t } : {}),",
                  "    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify(p) } }, cb);",
                  "",
                  "call('/api/v1/auth/login', {",
                  "    tenantSlug: pm.collectionVariables.get('tenantSlug'),",
                  "    email: pm.collectionVariables.get('email'),",
                  "    password: pm.collectionVariables.get('password')",
                  "}, null, (e1, r1) => {",
                  "    pm.test('phone signed in', () => pm.expect(r1.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "    const phone = r1.json();",
                  "    call('/api/v1/auth/logout', { refreshToken: laptop.refreshToken }, laptop.accessToken, (e2, r2) => {",
                  "        pm.test('laptop logged out', () => pm.expect(r2.code).to.eql(204));",
                  "        call('/api/v1/auth/token/refresh', { refreshToken: laptop.refreshToken }, null, (e3, dead) => {",
                  "            pm.test(\"laptop's session is gone\", () => pm.expect(dead.code).to.eql(401));",
                  "            call('/api/v1/auth/token/refresh', { refreshToken: phone.refreshToken }, null, (e4, alive) => {",
                  "                pm.test('phone is unaffected', () => pm.expect(alive.code).to.eql(200));",
                  "                const b = alive.json();",
                  "                pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken);",
                  "                pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken);",
                  "                pm.collectionVariables.set('accessTokenExpiresAt', Date.now() + b.expiresIn * 1000);",
                  "            });",
                  "        });",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const base = pm.collectionVariables.get('baseUrl');",
              "const post = (u, p) => ({ url: base + u, method: 'POST',",
              "    header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },",
              "    body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify(p) } });",
              "",
              "pm.sendRequest(post('/api/v1/tenants', {",
              "    tenantName: pm.collectionVariables.get('tenantName'),",
              "    tenantSlug: pm.collectionVariables.get('tenantSlug'),",
              "    adminEmail: pm.collectionVariables.get('email'),",
              "    adminPassword: pm.collectionVariables.get('password'),",
              "    firstName: 'Ada', lastName: 'Lovelace'",
              "}), () => {",
              "    pm.sendRequest(post('/api/v1/auth/login', {",
              "        tenantSlug: pm.collectionVariables.get('tenantSlug'),",
              "        email: pm.collectionVariables.get('email'),",
              "        password: pm.collectionVariables.get('password')",
              "    }), (e, r) => {",
              "        if (e || r.code !== 200) return;",
              "        const b = r.json();",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken);",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken);",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('accessTokenExpiresAt', Date.now() + b.expiresIn * 1000);",
              "        const d = (() => { try { return require('atob'); } catch (x) { return atob; } })();",
              "        const c = JSON.parse(d(b.accessToken.split('.')[1].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')));",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('tenantId', c.tenant_id);",
              "        pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', c.sub);",
              "    });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Access control",
      "description": "Role checks, and the rule that stops a tenant locking itself out.\n\nThe folder provisions an ordinary `TENANT_USER` automatically.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "A member cannot manage users",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "users"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sent with a `TENANT_USER` token against a `TENANT_ADMIN` endpoint.\n\nEnforced by `@PreAuthorize` on the controller as well as by the URL rules in `SecurityConfig` \u2014 path matching is easy to defeat by adding a route, a method annotation travels with the method.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"nope-{{$timestamp}}@acme.example\",\n  \"password\": \"another passphrase\",\n  \"firstName\": \"No\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Entry\",\n  \"roles\": [\n    \"TENANT_USER\"\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{memberAccessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('code is ACCESS_DENIED', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().code).to.eql('ACCESS_DENIED'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "A member can still reach their own account",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Default-deny does not mean deny-everything: self-service endpoints stay open to any authenticated caller.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{memberAccessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
